Task 2
User stories
As a student, I want to view my personal weekly timetable, so that I can plan so I can attend my classes at the right time.
As a student, I want to receive a notification when a class is rescheduled or cancelled, so that I don't waste a trip to school.
As a student, I want to export my timetable to my phones calendar app, so that I can have automatic offline access and reminders. Acceptance criteria: When class times change on the portal, then the user should be prompted to update or see the sync reflect the change in their calendar app.
As a student, I want to swap into an alternative lab or tutorial slot when my assigned one clashes with another commitment.
As a lecturer, I want to mark a specific class as cancelled or relocated so that students are immediately notified.Acceptance criteria: When the cancellaion or relocation is confirmed, then an automated email alert should be sent to the students.
As an administrator, I want to see which timetable slots are over capacity, so that I can reallocate rooms or split large classes before the semester begins.

INVEST
Each story is small and manageable, it clearly states the benefit of each need and the acceptance criterias are testable
