XP Practice: Continuous Integration
https://www.etsy.com/codeascraft/etsys-journey-to-continuous-integration-for-mobile-apps
In the blog, Etsy talks about how their engineering team adopted CI across thier mac min fllet using automated build pipelines and jenkins. By congifuring thier infrastructure to automatically trigger a build and execute test suites on every single Git push, Etsy successfully eliminated
compilation issues and missing files after code was commiteed. This allowed the developers to catch integration bug early and provide stable daily pre release builds across the company.

Continuous Integration supports the Scrum/Kanban workflow simulated in my trello board. We can ensure that user storeis moving into the "Done" column are automatically verified as Etsy did, without introducing any bugs. By automating builds and testing every Git Push, continuos integration prevents
any errors that may occur with late integration and it can also avoid manual verfication overhead. The lets the team to maintain sustainable speed in development and have high software quality.

